---
import SectionEyebrow from './SectionEyebrow.astro';

const migrationGuideUrl = 'https://github.com/cngxjs/compodocx/blob/develop/MIGRATION.md';
---

<section class="mx-auto max-w-6xl px-4 py-24" aria-labelledby="migration-heading">
  <SectionEyebrow text="From compodoc" />
  <div class="bg-cdx-bg-elevated border-cdx-primary mt-3 rounded-r-xl border-l-4 p-8 sm:p-10">
    <h2
      id="migration-heading"
      class="text-cdx-text text-2xl font-semibold tracking-tight sm:text-3xl"
    >
      Already on compodoc? Stay calm.
    </h2>
    <p class="text-cdx-text-secondary mt-3 max-w-2xl leading-relaxed">
      If you have a working compodoc setup, you can keep most of it. The CLI surface is the same,
      the internals are new. Most teams ship the migration in a single PR.
    </p>

    <ul class="mt-8 grid gap-6 md:grid-cols-3">
      <li class="text-sm">
        <h3 class="text-cdx-text text-base font-semibold">CLI alias works</h3>
        <p class="text-cdx-text-secondary mt-1.5 leading-relaxed">
          Your existing <code class="cdx-code">compodoc</code> scripts run unchanged. The binary registers
          both names.
        </p>
      </li>
      <li class="text-sm">
        <h3 class="text-cdx-text text-base font-semibold">JS template overrides</h3>
        <p class="text-cdx-text-secondary mt-1.5 leading-relaxed">
          Custom templates are now JS partials returning HTML. No Handlebars, no helpers registry.
          Just
          <code class="cdx-code">module.exports = (data, h) =&gt; '...'</code>.
        </p>
      </li>
      <li class="text-sm">
        <h3 class="text-cdx-text text-base font-semibold">
          <code class="cdx-code">migrate</code> sub-CLI
        </h3>
        <p class="text-cdx-text-secondary mt-1.5 leading-relaxed">
          Ports Handlebars templates and CSS automatically. Inspect first, then convert files or
          whole folders. You'll still want to review the diff.
        </p>
      </li>
    </ul>

    <a
      href={migrationGuideUrl}
      rel="noopener"
      target="_blank"
      class="text-cdx-primary hover:text-cdx-primary-hover mt-8 inline-flex items-center gap-1 text-sm font-medium"
    >
      Open MIGRATION.md
      <span aria-hidden="true">→</span>
      <span class="sr-only">(opens in new tab)</span>
    </a>
  </div>
</section>
